{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f13650232b3f8470","name":"card_event_battle_valor","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_battle_valor","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BATTLE VALOR","text":"Target unit becomes Veteran if able, then gets +2+4.","flavorText":"While it is difficult to provide precise numbers, machine gunners in bombers did contribute to shooting down enemy aircraft, especially when engaged in defensive actions. The primary objective of bomber gunners was to deter and suppress attacks rather than achieving high numbers of aerial victories. However, heroic actions of USAF machine gunners during WWII are numerous and what follows is an example. \r\n\r\nStaff Sergeant Maynard Harrison Smith served as a ball turret gunner on a B-17 Flying Fortress during WWII. On May 1, 1943, his aircraft was attacked by numerous German fighters during a mission over France. Smith's aircraft sustained heavy damage, and the tail section was severed, leaving the plane in imminent danger of breaking apart. Despite this, Smith remained at his position and provided covering fire in order to protect the crew. He refused to abandon his post until ordered to do so as the aircraft began to disintegrate. Smith's dedication and selflessness earned him the Medal of Honor. ","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_battle_valor","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battle_valor_title","SourceString":"BATTLE VALOR","LocalizedString":"BATTLE VALOR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battle_valor_text","SourceString":"Target unit becomes Veteran if able, then gets +2+4.","LocalizedString":"Target unit becomes Veteran if able, then gets +2+4."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battle_valor_history","S